{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"colloquial-key-groundhog","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nCreate can leave a real Jira issue without durable local identity. The coordinator must preserve write-ahead pending state and must never blind-replay an ambiguous create.\n\n## Outcome\nCoordinate the pre-create pending lifecycle intent and one budgeted Cloud/DC create call. A pending-save failure makes zero provider calls; ambiguous completion re-observes only through replay-safe identity/query seams or defers.\n\n## Plan\n1. Execute the versioned pending-binding intent durably before any create call. Return item-scoped persistence failure on save error.\n2. Call create once through the shared logical budget. Do not wrap the compound legacy create path.\n3. On timeout/connection loss, search only by replay-safe identity/query evidence. Return recovered success when the exact issue is proven; otherwise retain pending state and defer.\n4. Record returned Jira key immediately in the typed outcome for downstream containment; never delete a successful remote issue.\n5. Implement Cloud/DC failure cuts before save, during create, and immediately after key return.\n\n## Testing\nStateful fakes assert local bytes, provider call counts, known-key outcome, ambiguity, and no remote delete.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Failed pending save produces zero Jira calls and an item-scoped persistence outcome.\n- [ ] One physical create invocation issues exactly one provider create call.\n- [ ] Timeout/connection loss never blind-replays.\n- [ ] Exact replay-safe observation may recover success; inconclusive observation retains pending state and defers.\n- [ ] A returned Jira key is preserved in every later failure outcome.\n- [ ] No failure path deletes a successfully created Jira issue.\n\n## Out of scope\nLabel/property containment, local confirmation, restart convergence, and family cutover.","id":"d04c-c184-0b00-4a8a","parent_id":"59b0-d1b9-ad94-4339","priority":1,"tags":["rp03","create","reconciler","tdd"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-03 S4 T1 — Coordinate durable pending intent and one create attempt"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787028296100424001,"uuid":"11680e53-7604-4aaf-bbc5-6435311de9ab"}